  "limitations": [
    "Runtime measurements are expected to vary across hosts; exact structural values, raw historical measurements, and reported aggregates are preserved.",
    "The paper ZK evidence uses the seven-public-input legacy circuit snapshot, not the later eleven-public-input VBS migration circuit.",
    "Historical ZK scaling and backend CSVs retain aggregate measurements from twelve repetitions but not the individual per-repetition timing rows.",
    "Nitro payload sizes 1, 8, 32, and 128 MiB are directly measured; historical 256, 512, and 1024 MiB panel points are model projections from the measured plateau.",
    "Nitro worker counts 1, 2, and 4 are directly measured; counts 8 through 64 are model-calibrated projections.",
    "Protocol deviation detection is a seeded protocol-level simulation, not a hardware side-channel or platform-compromise experiment.",
    "The Base Sepolia campaign records one historical network state; reruns will have different fees and confirmation latencies."
  ]
}
